From 46a070457a8a847e6fbbdcd96f0bf03488d7d4e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon West <electrikjesus@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:54:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Taskbar: Read the applied retro style from
 Settings.Secure

The RetroStyle app runs as a system app on SELinux-enforcing builds,
where it can't set custom persist.* properties without extra policy.
It writes the resolved style to the secure setting retro_ui_applied
instead (layout, style, bar_apps, bar_buttons, ... as key=value
pairs), and the taskbar reads that once per process through
RetroUiApplied.

Change-Id: I905391bde510dfc965edbcde3055a841d1b22486
